/**
 * The scanned Krakel Orakel boards, as encoded dot positions.
 *
 * @module
 * @remarks
 * Generated data - do not edit by hand. Each string is one board: every dot is
 * four characters, two for the x coordinate and two for the y, each a 12-bit
 * value over a 64-character alphabet on the normalised 0..1 canvas. The decoder
 * and the tuning that goes with it live in `boards.ts`.
 *
 * The dots were traced from scans of the real game's printed drawing templates,
 * so a player draws along exactly the lines the physical board has.
 */

/** One encoded dot list per board, in the order the templates are numbered. */
